{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the tree of life in the midst of the garden.</b> Its Targum: 'וְאִילָן חַיַיָּא בִּמְצִיעוּת גִּנְּתָא וְאִילָן דְּאָכְלִין פֵּרוֹהִי חָכְמִין בֵּין טָב לְבִישׁ' — 'and the tree of life in the midst of the garden, and the tree whose fruit's eaters are wise to discern between good and evil.' He wished thereby to answer why the Holy One, blessed be He, did not warn Adam against both of them together — neither to eat of the tree of knowledge nor of the tree of life — but only concerning the tree of knowledge. For it is because the tree of life, by its very nature, is such that whoever eats of the tree itself lives forever, since it had no fruit at all and the taste of the tree was like the taste of its fruit. But the tree of knowledge had fruit desirable to the sight; all who eat of it would come to know between good and evil more than necessary. Therefore, before he ate of the tree of knowledge, there was no need to warn him about the tree of life, for it was not desirable to the sight, and he did not yet possess the discernment to perceive the benefit of eating of that tree, for it is merely a tree, and an ordinary animal does not eat wood but only something desirable to the sight that has fruit. But after he ate of the tree of knowledge, there was reason to fear lest he discern with his intellect the benefit of the tree of life and eat of it so as to live forever — therefore he was banished from there."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:45.957359383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}